    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the driveway entrance so responding units can confirm the correct property from the road.\n• Mark the driveway entrance with reflective posts on both sides to define the access point at night or in low-visibility conditions.\n• Keep the access drive clear of parked vehicles along its full length so emergency vehicles can reach both structures without obstruction.\n• Post the address visibly at the driveway entrance rather than only at the main residence, since the residence is not visible from the road on a long driveway.\n• Identify and communicate the location of the detached structure to responding units, as it may not be immediately visible upon arrival.\n• Keep a gate or entry point in the perimeter fencing unlocked or equipped with a key box so responders can enter without delay.\n• Maintain the vehicle parking area clear of equipment or stored items that would block a responding unit from turning around or repositioning near the main residence.\n• Trim any landscaping along the access drive that narrows the travel width or obscures sightlines for an approaching emergency vehicle.\n• Designate a flat, stable area near the structures where responding units can stage equipment without crossing soft ground or landscaped areas."
