    "recommendations": "• Remove shrubs that are growing directly next to the house.\n• Thin scattered trees near the structure to create open space between their canopies and the building.\n• Cut back ground vegetation growing close to the base of the structure.\n• Clear brush from the area immediately surrounding the house, working outward to create open separation between the brush and the building.\n• Mow or cut ground vegetation in the open green space areas nearest the structure to reduce the amount of low-lying plant material.\n• Trim any tree branches that hang over or touch the roof or walls of the structure.\n• Keep the single access route clear of overhanging branches and encroaching vegetation along both sides.\n• Remove dead or dry plant material from around any outbuildings or detached structures on the property.\n• Separate shrub groupings by thinning or removing individual plants so fire cannot move easily from one group to the next toward the house.\n• Keep the driveway surface and shoulders clear so emergency vehicles can pass through without obstruction."
